Originals: https://conjectures.io/v1/competitions/deflate/submissions/<id>/source

The DEFLATE encoder in src/encoder.rs is the competition's shared encoder
(https://github.com/conjectures-io/conjectures-optimisation-deflate,
validator/measure/src/deflate.rs), made incremental, with adaptive block splitting.

parsers/p85 builds on the competition's own `optimal-iter` example parser.

src/encoder.rs: the adaptive block splitting is new code; its idea (split where the
symbol statistics change, keep a split only if the exact cost drops) follows the block
splitter popularised by zopfli (https://github.com/google/zopfli).

The public API's shape (GzEncoder, ZlibEncoder, DeflateEncoder, finish, try_finish)
follows flate2 (https://github.com/rust-lang/flate2-rs) so it is familiar to Rust users;
no flate2 code is included in the library.

Formats: RFC 1950 (zlib), RFC 1951 (DEFLATE), RFC 1952 (gzip), SAM/BAM specification
section 4.1 (BGZF).
